::MCR_U04_L05_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U04_L05_Quiz_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.FL.11
Question:
Which response best supports this insurance skill: calculate annual premium cost?
{
=A. Compare premium, deductible, possible out-of-pocket cost, coverage, and risk.#Correct. Insurance decisions require cost comparison and risk interpretation, not just one price. 
~B. Choose only the lowest monthly premium.#The lowest premium can come with higher costs when care or claims happen. 
~C. Ignore the deductible.#The deductible affects possible out-of-pocket cost. 
~D. Assume insurance removes every cost.#Insurance can reduce risk, but plans still have limits and costs.
}


